      "writtenOn": "2026-08-20T15:22:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not sure about returning false for every other address family other than BGP-LU. Consider a plain IPv4 unicast route:\n1. Operator creates an app-rib IPv4 route with route-key \u003d \"my-route-1\" and prefix \u003d 10.0.0.0/24. ODL advertises 10.0.0.0/24 to the peer. The peer installs it.\n2. Operator edits that same entry, changing only prefix to 10.0.1.0/24. The route-key is untouched.\n3. Because the key didn\u0027t change, the datastore reports this as an in-place modification of one entry.\n4. Thanks to this commit ODL correctly notice the content changed and it advertises 10.0.1.0/24. The peer installs it.\n5. requiresWithdrawalOnReplace() is consulted at AdjRibOutListener.java:146. IPv4 unicast has no override, so it hits return false. No withdrawal is sent.\n6. Nothing in ODL advertises 10.0.0.0/24 any more, and the peer was never told to remove it. \n\nIt will stay leaked forever, right?",
